ideos leafy criticized  pokeman's content  her appearance and even went as far as  to say that she was  hiding a secret boyfriend from her fans  and that specific topic became  so popular after his videos that the  hashtag pokemaneboyfriend was trending  on twitter  and that prompted this joke from  pokemane who has said in the past that  she's not interested in making her love  life public on the internet leafy's  pokeman videos  all went viral and around that time  pokeman announced that she'd be taking a  long break from streaming and content  creation in general and then recently  pokeman released an apology video  discussing topics that range  all the way back to 2018 but she did  talk about some of leafy's criticisms  directly  specifically her relationship status and  his comments about her appearance  this video is to address recent comments  and criticisms that i've received  i know this video is long overdue i've  seen  a lot of people talk about the way that  i look recently  just want to put it out there i don't  think i'm the prettiest person in the  world  but i think that's okay everyone's  entitled to an opinion  i personally made the decision seven  years ago or whenever i got into  streaming that  i don't want my personal life to be a  part of my content and  that's just what i'm gonna stick by  until i and whoever i'm dating at  whatever time  decide otherwise that video was released  on august 18th  and then three days later on august 21st  leafy's entire youtube channel was gone  now youtube's policy when it comes to  violating their rules  is very similar to twitches that we talk  about all the time on this show  it's three strikes and then your own  each of the first two times you violate  a policy  you get warned and then the third time  the channel is just deleted  youtube cited quote multiple or severe  violations of youtube's policy  prohibiting content designed to harass  bully or threaten end quote as the  reason for leafy's ban  according to a tweet from slasher now  when the story about leafy's band first  broke  there was some speculation about whether  or not he was notified about his first  two strikes at all  a representative from youtube told julia  alexander a reporter from the verge that  quote  his channel was terminated because it  violated the company's harassment policy  three times over a period of 90 days  no specific videos were identified but  they did confirm  it's permanent when i asked specifically  about length of ban  end quote on august 21 after he was  banned leafy tweeted at youtube asking  how he could get his account reinstated  in response to the news another youtuber  kavos tweeted that leafy had never been  notified about his first two strikes at  all  and that his account had just been  banned out of nowhere leafy himself  also claimed he'd never been given any  strikes in a later comment that said  back on june 4th leafy actually tweeted  that he'd received two strikes on his  account for harassment there have been  some people commenting that those  strikes were reverted  but that hasn't been confirmed by leafy  himself or youtube at all on august 24th  leafy tweeted this still looking for his  account to be reinstated  and when team youtube responded he had  some choice words  as of recording this video leafy's  channel is still nowhere to be found on  youtube  and he's actually started to stream on  twitch so i guess he's trading places  with dr disrespect  now with this whole story in mind it's  worth noting that youtube has recently  made  massive changes to its policy  requirements for users  specifically the way that content  creators are supposed to treat  other content creators i've heard this  issue  in many different ways and i think we  have seen many  we've seen some high-profile examples  that we know have been  problematic and that has caused us to  take a really hard look  at our harassment policy as i'm sure  many of you know since like the  beginnin